WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.268 --> 00:00:02.549
Nina hurried into Kids Central.

2
00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:03.749
"Guess what!"

3
00:00:03.789 --> 00:00:04.189
she said.

4
00:00:04.229 --> 00:00:07.931
"My class went to the butterfly garden for Earth Day.

5
00:00:07.951 --> 00:00:13.813
Now I know everything about butterflies."

6
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:17.255
"Bugs are boring," Bobby said.

7
00:00:30.356 --> 00:00:31.377
Nina glared at him.

8
00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:34.278
"Butterflies are important!"

9
00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:37.440
Bobby shrugged.

10
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.502
"Boring." "Hi, everyone!"

11
00:00:41.862 --> 00:00:42.603
a voice said.

12
00:00:42.623 --> 00:00:46.004
"Cool! Mr.

13
00:00:46.084 --> 00:00:47.085
Dunn's here again!"

14
00:00:47.325 --> 00:00:48.126
Jason said.

15
00:00:48.146 --> 00:00:50.887
"Miss Shelly's out today," Mr.

16
00:00:50.947 --> 00:00:51.587
Dunn said.

17
00:00:51.607 --> 00:00:56.090
"So I'm here to celebrate Earth Day with everybody at Kids Central!"

18
00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:00.864
"In science we talked about recycling," Izzie said.

19
00:01:00.884 --> 00:01:03.845
"We made birdhouses," Jason said.

20
00:01:03.865 --> 00:01:08.447
"Well, we're going to plant a butterfly garden," Mr.

21
00:01:08.487 --> 00:01:09.127
Dunn said.

22
00:01:09.987 --> 00:01:10.807
Nina grinned.

23
00:01:10.827 --> 00:01:13.648
"I know a lot about butterflies.

24
00:01:14.508 --> 00:01:16.189
They pollinate flowers."

25
00:01:17.309 --> 00:01:18.530
Mr. Dunn smiled.

26
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.850
"They also keep plants healthy.

27
00:01:21.711 --> 00:01:22.691
Let's go outside.

28
00:01:23.191 --> 00:01:26.332
Ms. Folani said we can put the garden near the playground."

29
00:01:28.108 --> 00:01:30.610
The kids filled their water bottles and walked outside.

30
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:36.674
"I already prepared the soil for our garden," Mr.

31
00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:37.314
Dunn said.

32
00:01:38.115 --> 00:01:39.616
He pointed to a sunny spot.

33
00:01:39.636 --> 00:01:41.918
"Let's make a border with some rocks."

34
00:01:43.519 --> 00:01:45.700
After they finished making the border, Mr.

35
00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.161
Dunn showed the kids a drawing.

36
00:01:47.181 --> 00:01:49.783
"This shows where to plant things."

37
00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.525
Ethan picked up a plant.

38
00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.046
"What's this?"

39
00:01:54.066 --> 00:01:56.307
"Milkweed," Mr.

40
00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:56.968
Dunn said.

41
00:01:57.844 --> 00:01:59.225
"I know about that!"

42
00:01:59.545 --> 00:02:00.226
Nina said.

43
00:02:00.246 --> 00:02:05.449
"Some caterpillars eat milkweed before they turn into butterflies."

44
00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.191
Jason looked at the drawing.

45
00:02:08.211 --> 00:02:11.774
"The milkweed goes over there," he said.

46
00:02:11.794 --> 00:02:13.555
"I'll help Ethan plant it."

47
00:02:15.977 --> 00:02:17.798
Izzie and Nina looked at other flowers.

48
00:02:17.818 --> 00:02:21.800
"They're very colorful," Izzie said.

49
00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:26.644
"Butterflies see more colors than people do," Nina said.

50
00:02:27.008 --> 00:02:31.529
"They even see ultraviolet light that is invisible to us."

51
00:02:31.549 --> 00:02:36.311
"Let's plant these yellow flowers first," Izzie said.

52
00:02:36.331 --> 00:02:39.091
"These were a good choice, Mr.

53
00:02:39.171 --> 00:02:40.392
Dunn," Nina said.

54
00:02:40.412 --> 00:02:44.853
"The flowers are flat so the butterflies can reach the nectar."

55
00:02:46.013 --> 00:02:47.774
Mr. Dunn lifted his eyebrows.

56
00:02:47.794 --> 00:02:49.634
"I'm glad you approve."

57
00:02:50.894 --> 00:02:52.915
Bobby looked at two circles on the drawing.

58
00:02:52.935 --> 00:02:56.036
"Are those landing pads for butterflies?"

59
00:02:57.236 --> 00:02:58.337
Mr. Dunn laughed.

60
00:02:58.837 --> 00:03:01.118
"Nope. They're rocks."

61
00:03:02.618 --> 00:03:05.920
"Butterflies rest on flat rocks," Nina said.

62
00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.981
"The rocks give off heat in the morning.

63
00:03:09.621 --> 00:03:11.562
That helps the butterflies warm up.

64
00:03:12.242 --> 00:03:14.783
I learned—" "We know," Bobby said.

65
00:03:14.803 --> 00:03:18.545
"You learned everything at the butterfly garden."

66
00:03:23.086 --> 00:03:26.808
He put the two flat rocks in place while the others planted flowers.

67
00:03:32.096 --> 00:03:32.577
Then Mr.

68
00:03:32.617 --> 00:03:35.299
Dunn gave Bobby a shallow bowl and a bucket of sand.

69
00:03:35.319 --> 00:03:38.701
"This is for our butterfly puddler."

70
00:03:39.662 --> 00:03:42.304
Mr. Dunn explained how the butterfly puddler worked.

71
00:03:43.525 --> 00:03:45.027
Bobby filled the bowl with sand.

72
00:03:46.328 --> 00:03:49.010
Then he poured in water until it reached the top of the sand.

73
00:03:51.272 --> 00:03:52.653
Soon the planting was done.

74
00:03:53.673 --> 00:03:54.834
Ethan watered the garden.

75
00:03:59.358 --> 00:04:01.280
Then the kids sat under a tree, sipping water.

76
00:04:02.728 --> 00:04:05.751
"Now we wait for a butterfly," Mr.

77
00:04:05.791 --> 00:04:06.391
Dunn said.

78
00:04:06.411 --> 00:04:09.734
"I see one!"

79
00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:10.995
Nina cried.

80
00:04:11.015 --> 00:04:14.918
"It's going to our garden."

81
00:04:14.938 --> 00:04:18.321
"Awesome," Bobby said.

82
00:04:18.341 --> 00:04:21.644
"It's drinking from the butterfly puddler!"

83
00:04:21.664 --> 00:04:24.126
"Huh?" Nina said.

84
00:04:24.146 --> 00:04:26.928
"What's a butterfly puddler?"

85
00:04:27.228 --> 00:04:28.249
Bobby smiled.

86
00:04:28.269 --> 00:04:31.192
"It's like a birdbath for butterflies.

87
00:04:32.064 --> 00:04:34.547
They can stand on sand while they drink water."

88
00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:37.510
"Oh." Nina flushed.

89
00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:39.412
"That's cool.

90
00:04:40.132 --> 00:04:43.556
I guess I don't know everything about butterflies!"
